<title>SINGAPORE: MidEast crude term prices update.</title>
<headline>MidEast crude term prices update.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Middle East oil companies have cut their crude term monthly prices for June, narrowing the differentials of their crudes against Dubai crude.</p>
<p>The following table shows the latest official selling prices and their differentials to the quoted Dubai average for June of 17.28, which traders use as a guage of relative value.</p>
<p>				(Prices are per barrel)</p>
<p>						   Differential to Dubai</p>
<p>		   Jun     May     Change    Jun     May    Change</p>
<p>QATAR MARINE  $17.72  $19.28  -$1.56   +$0.44  +$0.73  (-$0.29)</p>
<p>QATAR LAND    $18.05  $19.58  -$1.53   +$0.77  +$1.03  (-$0.26)</p>
<p>OMAN	    $17.75  $19.25  -$1.50   +$0.47  +$0.70  (-$0.23)</p>
<p>MURBAN	  $18.35  $20.00  -$1.65   +$1.07  +$1.45  (-$0.43)</p>
<p>LOWER ZAKUM   $18.35  $20.05  -$1.70   +$1.07  +$1.50  (-$0.43)</p>
<p>UMM SHAIF     $18.10  $19.75  -$1.65   +$0.82  +$1.20  (-$0.38)</p>
<p>UPPER ZAKUM   $17.35  $18.70  -$1.35   +$0.07  +$0.15  (-$0.08)</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
